00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:05.080
Magic mushrooms are going to be decriminalized. In Denver voters electing to make the city the first...

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:09.680
We've become the first city in America to decriminalize magic mushrooms.

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:16.180
On May 7th, 2019, Denver voted to become the first city in America to decriminalize magic mushrooms.

00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:21.220
On the night of the victory, campaign organizer Kevin Matthews announced that he was taking the movement

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:26.480
nationwide. Our success tonight will be a signal to the rest of the country that

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:30.840
these kinds of campaigns are viable, that if individuals choose to

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:34.160
unite behind the idea of changing the laws around psilocybin,

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:40.100
it can happen.  A few weeks later Oakland decriminalized all psychedelic plants and fungus.

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:44.700
That motion passes unanimously.

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:48.980
Santa Cruz, California followed in Oakland's footsteps on January 29th,

00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:53.980
and now statewide efforts are underway in Washington State, Oregon, and California.

00:00:53.980 --> 00:00:58.440
When it comes to psychedelics we feel people should have the freedom of choice

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:00.940
to choose what they want and in essence
cognitive liberty.

00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:07.100
Ryan Dunevar is the head of Decriminalize California, which is looking to take the movement one step further.

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:11.560
The group seeks to convince California voters not only to eliminate laws that prohibit

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:14.380
the possession and consumption of psychedelic mushrooms,

00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:17.940
but  to create a legal framework for commercial sales.

00:01:17.940 --> 00:01:22.800
We realized, alright, let's make sure nobody else goes to jail for this. Let's give it a proper regulated system

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:26.620
and let's make sure nobody creates a bureau cannabis controlled model for mushrooms, because

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:31.760
that'll just screw up everything. And we realized in order to do that you'd actually have to,

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:35.440
in essence, legalize sales.

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:40.900
But Dunevar's approach is proving controversial within the movement among those who seek decriminalization

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:46.880
as a path to communing with nature. We led from a place of love that is we didn't push commodification,

00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:51.840
we pushed equitable access and just decriminalizing our relationship with nature.

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:57.840
Carlos Plazola is the head of Decriminalize Nature in Oakland, which is geared towards removing barriers

